        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Shiraz</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">693 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Shiraz was founded or restored in 693 by Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Thaqafi, brother of the Umayyad viceroy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hajjaj-ibn-yusuf">al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf</a>, or by the latter's kinsman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-qasim">Muhammad ibn Qasim</a>; Elamite tablets of 2000 BCE name an earlier city called Tiraziš.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On a plain at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros Mountains</a>, 1,500 metres above sea level, in the north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars province</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, with a seasonal river, the Dry River, flowing through its northern part.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Elamite name Tiraziš; capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saffarid-dynasty">Saffarids</a> and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adud-al-dawla">Adud al-Dawla</a>'s library and hospital; the poets Saadi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafez">Hafez</a>; the philosopher Mulla Sadra; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan Zand</a>'s capital; the city where the Báb declared his mission in 1844</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Shiraz is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars province</a> and the fifth most populous city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>.</span></div>
